## MVP Scope

### MVP Must Include

1. Custom GPT accepts image or text input.
2. Backend processes notebook task content.
3. Task extraction works on clear notebook pages.
4. Date is detected if present.
5. Tasks are categorized into Personal / Business-Kouch / Unclear.
6. Tasks are saved into Google Sheets.
7. User can query old tasks.
8. User can update statuses.
9. Data remains available after chat deletion.
10. Optional Notion sync works as a readable dashboard.

### MVP Must Not Include

- advanced OCR optimization
- mobile app
- multi-user permissions
- advanced analytics
- reminder engine
- complex deduplication
- too many categories
- full project management features

### Best MVP Interaction Pattern

1. User uploads notebook page.
2. System extracts proposed tasks.
3. System shows them for confirmation.
4. Approved tasks are saved to Google Sheets.
5. Optional mirror is sent to Notion.
6. Later updates and queries use stored task records.

That confirmation step is important because it prevents bad records from entering the database.

